        <p>
          <alert>John Meier</alert> 
          
          earned his BA from the University of Virginia in 1987, and his
          MS and Ph.D.  from Cornell University in 1990 and 1992,
          respectively.
        </p>
        <p>
          John joined Lafayette College in <m>1992</m>. He was promoted
          to Associate Professor in <m>1999</m>, to Professor <m>2004</m>. In <m>2019</m> he was became the Provost of Lafayette College. John  has been
          an active member of  EPaDel since <m>2003</m>, serving as
          President in <m>2005</m>, <m>2006</m>, and <m>2007</m>. He was also the <m>2010</m> recipient of the James P. Crawford Teaching Award.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li xml:id="StyerBio">
