      </aside>
      <p>
        <alert> Lisa Marano </alert> 
        was born in Camden, New Jersey, and attended Rider
        College with a major in Mathematics and Secondary Education
        before doing her graduate work at Lehigh University. In 2002,
        she completed her PhD in Probability and Mathematical Finance
        under the direction of Vladimir Dobric.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lisa took a tenure-track position at LaSalle University
        immediately upon graduation from Lehigh University, but the
        following year she moved into a tenure-track position at West
        Chester University. She has remained at WCU to this date,
        moving through the academic ranks and founding the West
        Chester University Actuarial Science program. She is currently
        Associate Dean for the College of Mathematics and Sciences.
      </p>  
<p>
      Within EPADEL, Lisa served in the elected positions of Vice
      Chair, Chair, and Section Representative after serving in the
      Executive Committee from 2005 – 2007 as an at-large
      member. Before that she served as one of the coordinators of
      Section NExT. In that role, along With Kate McGivney, she
      secured funding for joint programming with AMATYC’s Project
      ACCCESS.
</p>
      <p>
        Lisa has the distinction of being the last occupant of two
        positions within EPADEL. While she was serving as Section
        President in 2008 EPADEL's By Laws were updated and the title
        was changed to "Chair."  She was also serving as Section
        Governor when the 2017 MAA By Laws update changed that title
        to "Section Representative to MAA Congress." Starting in 2018
        Lisa has been a member of the MAA's Board of Directors as a
        consequence of serving as the Chair of the Committee on
        Sections.
